{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Epic 7e9e: BLOCK G6 CRITICAL — the D6 in-scope claim (reading the active OTel span aligns the gateway header with rebar's exported Langfuse spans) is NOT achieved at the described read point. rebar opens no root span, so at the gate boundary nothing is recording and the id mints; tracing.py's per-candidate spans open later inside each model request, each its own trace root, so their trace_ids never equal the header value under fan-out. Claim corrected in epic + 6cd0 rather than reverting the read: reading an existing span is still correct and free when an enclosing span exists, but the epic now states plainly that header/span alignment requires the run-level root span and is the deferred follow-on. This reconciles the conformance finding with the user's B1-now/B2-later scope."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787723077045644001,"uuid":"329de231-dd8c-4fa1-8041-94f2f92ac366"}